.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 431 AM PDT Mon Aug 10 2026

Coastal stratus and fog /MVFR-IFR-LIFR/ continue to redevelop and
onshore winds are at least partially ushering stratus and fog inland
this morning. More recently the marine layer is showing signs of
deepening to 1300 to 1800 feet. Stratus and fog will mix out by
late morning with VFR prevailing through the afternoon. Stratus
and fog /MVFR-IFR-LIFR/ redevelop tonight and Tuesday morning.

Vicinity of SFO...Stratus is currently north of SFO. VFR is forecast
to continue at the terminal. West to northwest wind 5 to 15 knots
except 15 to 25 knots in the afternoon and evening.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Stratus /IFR-LIFR/ will mix out to VFR by
late morning with VFR continuing through the afternoon. Stratus /IFR-
LIFR/ redevelops and moves inland tonight and Tuesday morning. West
to northwest winds 5 to 15 knots.

