.MARINE...
(Today through Saturday)
Issued at 407 AM PDT Mon Aug 10 2026

Fresh to strong northwest winds will persist through the middle
of the week with rough seas up to 12 feet over the northern outer
waters and occasionally the inner waters north of Point Reyes. The
San Pablo, Suisun Bays and the Delta will continue to see gusty
onshore winds through early this evening. The long period
southerly swells around 15 seconds will continue through much of
the work  week.

&&

.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 1205 AM PDT Mon Aug 10 2026

Elevated fire weather conditions persist Monday across the higher
terrain due to an increase in onshore flow on the heels of very hot
and dry conditions. Slow improvement is expected with temperatures
still 10 degrees above normal and minimum relative humidity of 15%-
30% Monday afternoon. Gusts up to 30 mph can be expected through
gaps/passes and across ridgelines; namely, the Delta, Altamont Pass,
Pacheco Pass, and Interior Mountains of Monterey and San Benito
Counties. Moderate overnight recovery is expected Monday night;
however, the highest terrain of the Central Coast will likely remain
poor.

